s how to meet mandate. So applicability 4.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... Reference class: responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Parallel workstream budgeting? Might be common project management. Probably common, mundane. Originality 1 = common, mundane, boring. Evidence: Carving a compliance workstream with percentage FTE allocation is standard project-management practice for regulated engineering.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm. Paradigm breaking 4, stretching 3, slightly stretching 2, preserving 1. This introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. Slightly paradigm stretching? It introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. That's level 2. Could be paradigm preserving? Standard compliance practice. The description of slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Yes fits. Score 2.\n\nImplementability: degree to which idea can be easily implemented. Revised internal template, allocate 12-18% FTE, track quarterly, backfill gaps. Some changes, reasonably feasible. Level 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or easy? Might need org change. I'd say 3. Evidence: Revising a planning template and reallocating a modest share of engineering FTE is a manageable organizational change without requiring new technology.\n\nAcceptability: degree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms. Score 4. Evidence: Dedicated compliance budgeting aligns with responsible R&D norms and regulatory expectations.\n\nProvide output format. Need echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably as lines.\n\nLet's produce JSON? Probably plain text.\n\nReturn rating of proposal,