y politically acceptable.\n4 common strategies that violate no norms\nThis is standard engineering, acceptable. So 4.\n\nEvidence: Embedding engineers to add telemetry uses existing monitoring stack and respects normal sprint cycles with no legal or normative conflict.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\nIt says minimal refactor cost, incremental overhead, working inside normal sprint cycles. Seems easy? Embedding three engineers per group over two quarters might be resource intensive but still feasible. Might be 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible. Or 4 = easy low cost? \"minimal refactor cost\" suggests easy. But embedding three engineers per group is not trivial. Could be 3.\n\nDefinition: 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n\nI think it's somewhat more than non-radical. It's embedding engineers. I'd give 3.\n\nEvidence: Adding structured telemetry via existing monitoring stack within normal sprints is reasonably feasible though it requires dedicated engineering time over two quarters.\n\nImplementability =3\n\nReturn JSON? Probably format with fields.\n\nNeed echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProvide output.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1463\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality:1\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft succinct sentences.\n\nProceed.",
