rectly enforce logging-scheme design and retention verification required by Article 12 for high-risk systems.\n\neffectiveness: degree will solve problem. 4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). Will it solve? It prevents late rework and allocates effort; helps meet logging mandate but does it guarantee compliance? Likely contributes. Might be 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution, partial. The proposal ensures checkpoints but doesn't guarantee logs are technically correct. Might be partial solution. I'd say 3.\n\nEvidence: Early checkpoints reduce rework and improve traceability but do not by themselves guarantee that the logging is technically sufficient for Article 12's automatic recording requirements.\n\nReturn rating echo id.\n\nFormat: need <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably lines.\n\nOutput JSON? Instruction says return rating echo its id exactly. For each subscale give ... first and then... Probably plain text.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P2019\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 1\netc.\n\nMake sure order: originality, paradigm_relatedness, acceptability, implementability, applicability, effectiveness.\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's craft succinct sentences.\n\n",
